          "text": "The image is a side-by-side composite figure. The left panel is a photograph showing a metallic mounting bracket or traversing mechanism, to which two dark cylindrical camera units are attached. Cables run from the units, and the structure appears to be mounted on a vertical beam or inside a wind-tunnel-like setting. The right panel is a schematic line drawing: a large circle crossed by horizontal and vertical axes; a green line runs from the circle center to its right edge. An angle arc between the upper vertical axis and the green line is labelled 30.65°. A black arrowhead marks the point where the green line meets the circle. A dashed arrow labelled 5.6m points outward from that location toward a small rectangular symbol resembling a camera. These elements relate to the caption in the supplied context about PIV cameras and viewing direction, but the image itself only visibly contains the photo, the circle diagram, the angle, the distance label, and the arrow/camera symbol.\nPIV 相机 拍摄方向 光片 角度 示意图 风洞 测量 安装支架\nPIV cameras viewing direction light sheet angle schematic wind tunnel measurement mounting bracket\n30.65°\n5.6m\nTwo dark camera units are mounted on a metallic bracket/traverse in the left photograph.\nIn the right schematic, a green line extends from the center of the circle to its right edge.\nThe angle between the upper vertical axis and the green line is labelled 30.65°.\nA dashed line labelled 5.6m extends from the point where the green line meets the circle to a small camera-like symbol.",
